I am at the office.
The new project starts today.
The team manager, Suresh, calls me into his cabin.
I go inside and sit down.
"Welcome to the new team, Maya," he says.
"We are starting a big project."
"Has Maya done similar work before?" he asks.
I smile.
I have done this kind of work in Mexico.
"Yes, I have worked on two similar projects," I reply.
"I have made software for shops."
He nods happily.
"That is very good," Suresh says.
"Your experience will be very useful to us."
He gives me a file.
"Please read these details."
"Okay, I will read it," I say.
I am very happy.
My old experience is suited for this new job.
